      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 3.03,
          "en": "Now, for this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.03,
          "end": 5.31,
          "en": "I prepared another starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.31,
          "end": 8.19,
          "en": "a local and a CodeSandbox version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.19,
          "end": 11.1,
          "en": "The CodeSandbox version is already up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.1,
          "end": 13.89,
          "en": "For the local version, you need to run npm install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 16.95,
          "en": "once you downloaded and extracted the attachment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.95,
          "end": 18.603,
          "en": "and then npm run dev.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.53,
          "end": 24.53,
          "en": "And once you did that, you should see this website here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.54,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "a non-functional Placepicker website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 32.16,
          "en": "where the idea is that by the end of this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 36.3,
          "en": "you can pick and select places and unselect them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 39.24,
          "en": "but, and that's the important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.24,
          "end": 41.7,
          "en": "compared to an earlier course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.7,
          "end": 44.88,
          "en": "here in this version of this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.88,
          "end": 48.48,
          "en": "all the data will be fetched from a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.48,
          "end": 51.6,
          "en": "And, for example, when we pick a place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.6,
          "end": 53.37,
          "en": "when we make a selection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.37,
          "end": 57.963,
          "en": "that change will also be stored on a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.963,
          "end": 60.84,
          "en": "And therefore, this starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.84,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "also comes with a backend folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "that contains a separate backend web API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 71.91,
          "en": "A backend project, not written in React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.91,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "but instead, in this case with NodeJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.24,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "But as mentioned before, you could build such a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 81.003,
          "en": "with any programming language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "Now, this here is a very simple dummy backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 87.27,
          "en": "And in the end, the entire backend logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.27,
          "end": 90.6,
          "en": "lives in this app.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.6,
          "end": 94.5,
          "en": "Here, I'm setting up a simple backend API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "where I'm accepting certain kinds of requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 100.92,
          "en": "because remember, that's what I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.92,
          "end": 105.66,
          "en": "the backend controls which kind of requests are allowed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.66,
          "end": 109.71000000000001,
          "en": "and blocks other requests that are not allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 112.5,
          "en": "Hence, ensuring that users can only do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.5,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "what you want them to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 118.77000000000001,
          "en": "And here in this dummy backend, in this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 123.77,
          "en": "I, for example, allow GET HTTP requests to my backend URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 128.91,
          "en": "and then /places to fetch available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.91,
          "end": 131.16,
          "en": "that could be picked by users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.16,
          "end": 134.04,
          "en": "And then I have some user-places routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.04,
          "end": 137.22,
          "en": "that can be used to get places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.22,
          "end": 140.28,
          "en": "stored by the users of this website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.28,
          "end": 143.493,
          "en": "and to change those stored places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 147,
          "en": "Now, as mentioned, this is a simple backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 151.29,
          "en": "And, for example, here, all users from all over the world",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.29,
          "end": 153.78,
          "en": "would share the same user data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.78,
          "end": 158.46,
          "en": "but it's a great example to get started with data fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 163.06,
          "en": "Now, in case the terms GET request or URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.07,
          "end": 167.16,
          "en": "are terms that don't tell you anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.16,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "I strongly recommend that you revisit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 174.84,
          "en": "some web development and web functionality basics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.84,
          "end": 178.23,
          "en": "because you absolutely should know terms like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.23,
          "end": 182.22,
          "en": "And attached, you therefore find some helpful resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.22,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "that help you revisit those concepts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 187.38,
          "en": "In this section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.38,
          "end": 190.08,
          "en": "we'll not focus on the backend code though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 190.08,
          "end": 193.35,
          "en": "because this is not a backend development course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.35,
          "end": 196.17000000000002,
          "en": "Instead, we'll just use this dummy backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.17000000000002,
          "end": 200.13,
          "en": "to connect to it from inside this React application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.13,
          "end": 203.28300000000002,
          "en": "which you'll also find in this starting project.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
